hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1137","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, Abu Dawud told us, Shu’bah told us, he said: I heard Yazid bin Khumayr, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Abi Qais. He says: Aisha said to me: “Do not neglect the night prayer, for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not neglect it, and when he was sick or lazy, he would He prayed while sitting.” Ali bin Muslim praised him and said: If he is bored or lazy. Abu Bakr said: This Sheikh Abdullah is the one I have, whom the Egyptians and the Levant call him: Abdullah bin Abi Qais. He narrated from him. Muawiya bin Saleh news"
"1138","He narrated, and Abu Bakr bin Abdullah bin Abi Maryam narrated, saying: Abdullah bin Abi Qais told me, on the authority of the mothers of the believers. They told him that God Almighty directed his Prophet to a guide, so he said to them: Guide me to what God guided his Prophet to, so they said: “Indeed, God His Prophet instructed him to pray the night prayer.” Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Abu Al-Mughirah told us, Abu Bakr, meaning Ibn Abi Maryam, Abdullah told me, Ibn Yahya said, and he is Ibn Abi Qais"
